The reusable dzil-binary workflow records asset hashes only for releases and does not persist the full source commit, resolved workflow commit, actual runner image/version, OS/arch/ABI and probe hashes together. Add a machine-readable provenance artifact for probe and release runs so briefing k7 can verify its approved standalone-binary trust contract. Do not publish or retag without separate maintainer authorization.

From briefing k7 Task 7 review (2026-11-18): (1) dzil-binary.yml declares input bundle_ref with default binary-v1 and checks out its scripts (plan.pl, build-leg.sh, build-perl.sh, publish.pl) at that ref, so a caller that pins uses: ...@<sha> still runs mutable-tag code unless it also passes bundle_ref: <same sha>. briefing will pass it explicitly; consider defaulting bundle_ref to the called workflow's own commit. (2) The Linux smoke runs inside docker run with only SMOKE/BIN in the environment, so GITHUB_SHA, ImageOS/ImageVersion and RUNNER_* are not visible to the smoke script; a provenance manifest has to be written by the workflow (outside the container) from the run context.

Maintainer decisions 2026-11-20: (1) release runs persist the manifest both as a run artifact and as a release asset provenance.json (not listed in SHA256SUMS, so briefing's pin import is unaffected); probe runs as artifact only. (2) bundle_ref defaults to the called workflow's own commit, resolved once in the plan job from the run record (referenced_workflows) and handed to every job; an explicit bundle_ref still wins; an unresolvable commit fails the run loudly, no silent fallback to binary-v1. Sequenced after k34 (same files).

Design round 2026-11-20 (worker, read-only; design doc handed to test-writer/worker). Maintainer decisions: D1 the workflow commit comes from job.workflow_sha (GitHub, 2026-09), not the run record — no new permissions for callers, empty value fails loudly; bundle_ref default becomes '' = that commit, pinned once in plan (bundle_commit output) and used by every other job; guard: job.workflow_repository must be Getty/p5-dist-zilla-pluginbundle-author-getty. D2 strict: new provenance job (probe + release) merges per-job key=value parts (facts.sh, build-leg.sh provenance) via provenance.pl, cross-checks all hashes/commits; publish needs it, verifies the manifest against SHA256SUMS and uploads provenance.json; runner image facts required on host jobs, null allowed in container build legs. Artifact names provenance.plan / provenance.build.<platform> / provenance.smoke.<n> / <dist>-<version>.provenance avoid every download pattern.

